					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/monteparnas" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2926286); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2926286&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973155" alt="Monteparnas" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2926286)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/monteparnas" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2926286); return false;" >Monteparnas</a></span> <span class="odate time_1520034888 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Mar 2018 23:54</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3726942">
									

<p>Remember that the document is non-anomalous. It won't attract the attention of other entities, only define you as a target for the Foundation alone. And even then, only at the direct instruction of the O5, since the everyday Foundation crew won't instantly know of this change.</p>
<p>As someone that works for a huge company (the biggest bank of my country), I know that this kind of document is a very real thing, but with almost no effect on activities except on a very broad and philosophical sense.</p>
<p>The &quot;I still love you&quot; line probably refers to every anomaly, not to any reader in particular.</p>

