			<div class="content" id="post-content-3676165">
									

<p>Just a question: when you clicked &quot;ACCESS SCP-001&quot; what did you write?</p>
<p>I did the most obvious and crazy route, that is; I typed some deep philosophical shit.</p>
<p>&quot;The true question is how does it howl? Sure it might be able to howl, and you can very clearly observe it's howl just by hearing it, then scouting your six mile radius to check for any possible wolves, coyotes, or some canine sort of predator. Then you are sure that it was the black moon howling, not the wolves. However, how DOES it howl should be the bigger question. A black moon is not exactly organic, I severely doubt you can go up to one and say &quot;Good evening, sir, may I excavate into your body to examine your insides and see if you have vocal chords?&quot; Much less if one is sentient at all (And I doubt the black moon will exactly appreciate your question, unless it is a man of extreme science). So how DOES it howl is the true question. Is it anomalous? Of course if it is, contact your Site Director to inform him or her that you have possibly found a new SCP, that is; a dark moon orbiting a certain planet that, without it's own vocal chords, can vocalize a howl. And, who knows? Perhaps it can cause a XK-Class End-of-The-World Scenario, you might just save existence by reporting it. Think on this question, for this is the bigger picture.&quot;</p>
<p>Anyways as for the file itself&#8230; hmm&#8230; I'm not sure I understood it that well, I'm not really that big of an open, immersive mind, however, I do enjoy a good meta-mindfuck. So, thank you for that.<br />
But from what I do see. It looks like a good article, so kudos to you. +1</p>

							</div>

								
